      "name": "Traffic Volume Counts (Historical)",
      "description": "This is static historical dataset. New York City Department of Transportation (NYC DOT) uses Automated Traffic Recorders (ATR) to collect traffic sample volume counts at bridge crossings and roadways. These counts do not cover the entire year, and the number of days counted per location may vary from year to year.\n\nFor a current feed of Automated Traffic Volume Counts, see: https://data.cityofnewyork.us/Transportation/Automated-Traffic-Volume-Counts/7ym2-wayt",
